! The phase plan

''Lares (Pedagogue).'' Ordered by Breach-Watch's triage and by what each step's red can actually witness. Every step is red-first and every step ships a CONTROL, because three of the cures below go green on a catastrophe if the control is missing. Estimates are spirit-hours, honest, including the collide step that each red owes.

!! Phase 0 · collide the leans before building on them — 1.5 h

* ''RED (probe, expected to REFUTE):'' `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/root-law-one-spelling.test.ts` gains a vector asserting that a root re-placed from its records after a child's tombstone still carries `<<~ kahea ahu #/b>>`. Written as a plain `test` that PASSES on the current tree, with a comment naming the lean it refutes: `syncer-back-parity.mem` `#/leans`, "which would also close (c′)".
* ''CURE:'' none. This phase moves no source.
* ''CONTROL:'' the same probe over a root whose child STANDS — the marker expands, proving the probe reads the recompose and not an accident of the fixture.
* ''WITNESS:'' `pnpm -C packages/lararium-tw5 vitest run tests/root-law-one-spelling.test.ts`. If the probe fails (the marker DOES drop), phase 3 changes shape and the operator is told before anything else moves.

!! Phase 1 · the root law gets one spelling — closes (b′) — 2.5 h

* ''RED (unit):'' `tests/root-law-one-spelling.test.ts` — (i) `framedRootOf` over a slot child's fields (title `lar:///t/a#/a`, carrier type, `$fragment-parent` set, a framed head in its text) answers null; (ii) `nativeDoorGate` over that same body as TiddlyWeb JSON answers `pass`, never `refuse`.
* ''CURE:'' `packages/lararium-tw5/src/place-meme.ts:112` — `framedRootOf` reads the root law rather than the mark alone: a title carrying `#`, or fields carrying `$fragment-parent`, answers null. Spelled by reading the predicate `isMemeRoot` already reads (`place-meme.ts:216-223`), never a second copy — that warning is the reason this seam exists.
* ''CONTROL (three, all must stay green):'' a true framed root still answers its head URI; `nativeDoorGate` still refuses a true framed root with 422; the charm still re-addresses a true root to `/memes/`.
* ''WITNESS:'' unit suite; then `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts:226` flips `test.fails` → `test` with its assertion REWRITTEN — it must assert the wire read `PUT /recipes/default/tiddlers/lar%3A%2F%2F%2Ft%2Fa%23%2Fa -> 204` (not merely that the bad title is absent), because the old assertion cannot tell this cure from a stall. Plus a new e2e ''anti-stall control'': a save issued AFTER the child's save lands its own 2xx — the one vector that proves `syncer.js:436` did not fire. Run on the fork and again under `LARES_TW5_JS` against pristine 5.4.1.

!! Phase 2 · the fragment door walls itself — 1 h

* ''RED (unit):'' `tests/meme-routes.test.ts` — `PUT /bags/default/memes/lar/t/a%23/a` answers 400, body naming the single-hash law.
* ''CURE:'' `src/routes/put-meme.ts` — a URI carrying `#` refuses at the same place `memeUriOfParams` already refuses a malformed escape (`put-meme.ts:98-103`).
* ''CONTROL:'' a root URI still lands 200; `GET` and `DELETE` on the same fragment path answer as they do today (this step touches PUT alone).
* ''WITNESS:'' unit; and the Phase 1 e2e re-run unchanged — after Phase 1 no stock client addresses this door, so the wall must cost the syncer NOTHING. If any e2e vector moves, Phase 1 was incomplete.

!! Phase 3 · the group arrives whole — closes (d′) — 4 h

* ''RED (e2e):'' `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts:273` stands as written; it goes green on the cure.
* ''CURE:'' a new route skin (`src/routes/native-skinny-door.ts`), `module-type: route`, priority 110 on stock's own `/^\/recipes\/default\/tiddlers.json$/`. It wraps `state.sendResponse`, delegates to `$:/core/modules/server/routes/get-tiddlers-json.js`, and re-inflates entries whose record carries `$fragment-parent` with their `text` before the body leaves. Stock's filter, its `ExternalFilters` guard and its `SyncSystemTiddlersFromServer` clause are never re-derived (`get-tiddlers-json.js:22-33`).
* ''CONTROL (three):'' a plain tiddler still arrives SKINNY in the same answer (`text === undefined` at the client); a meme ROOT still arrives skinny (only children fatten); and stock's `filter`/`exclude` query parameters still govern — a request carrying an explicit `exclude=` is honoured unchanged.
* ''MEASURE AND REPORT, not assert:'' the answer's byte size before and after, on the lab's fixture, so the operator can rule the dial against a number instead of a worry.
* ''WITNESS:'' unit vectors for the skin (delegation · the re-inflate · the three controls); the e2e on fork AND pristine. ''No docker leg'' — see #/refusals.

!! Phase 4 · the member's death gets named — (c′) — 2.5 h, and BLOCKED on the operator

* ''RED (e2e):'' `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts:242` inverts — from `test.fails` asserting the residue is absent, to `test` asserting the residue STANDS and is marked. The inversion IS the ruling; it cannot be written before the operator rules.
* ''CURE (under the (c′-2) lean):'' `packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/ahu-template-html.tid:4` — the section distinguishes three states of an empty body: //unresolved// (no record stands at the child's address), //arriving// (a record stands with no text), //empty// (a record stands with empty text). Spelled the way `tiddlers/kahea-template-html.tid:4` already spells a missing target. This single step also delivers (d′-2)'s cord — the two leans collide on this one file and land together or not at all.
* ''CONTROL:'' a section with a present, filled child renders exactly as it does today — asserted against the existing shelf-render census (`tests/shelf-render-census.test.ts`), which must not move.
* ''WITNESS:'' render census + a render unit over the three states; the e2e vector at `:242`.
* ''NOT IN THIS PHASE:'' any door change, any hash motion, any binding of `<<~?`.

!! Phase 5 · the ungated child — seam (b), the residue Phase 1 leaves — 4 h, and LAST

* ''RED (unit):'' `tests/meme-backstop.test.ts` — a slot child modified on the `change` bus, whose `$fragment-parent` names a standing root, causes the ROOT to re-place; a child whose parent does not stand causes nothing.
* ''CURE:'' `src/modules/meme-backstop.ts:66` widens from "a record `framedRootOf` names" to "a record `framedRootOf` names, OR a record whose `$fragment-parent` names a standing root" — the latter re-placing the ROOT. Node-only, which is where every browser client's saves land, so the law reaches every client (`#/charm-reach`).
* ''THE RISK, NAMED BEFORE IT IS BUILT:'' the re-place writes the children, `change` fires for them, and the backstop fires again. The existing `inFlight` set (`meme-backstop.ts:60`) is per-title and cleared in `finally` — it does not stop this. An echo law is REQUIRED, and it must be a SET or a COUNT, never a flag: `outbound-bridge.mem:78` measured that `change` dispatches AFTER the applying guard lowers, and `syncer.js:254-264` is stock's own answer (stamp the changeCount in the same synchronous stretch). The rhyme to copy is `recordLandedPacks` (`packages/lares-cli/src/ingest-core.ts:201`).
* ''CONTROL (three, the third is the whole phase):'' a plain tiddler's change fires nothing; a child under an absent root fires nothing; ''the re-place's OWN writes fire nothing'' — a vector that counts backstop invocations across one child save and asserts exactly one.
* ''WITNESS:'' unit; then e2e vector (b) at `:203` tightened — after a child save the server log carries exactly ONE `[memetic-wikitext]` line and the root's record re-cut.

!! The whole, ordered

| # | phase | closes | spirit-hours | blocked on |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | collide the leans | — | 1.5 | nothing |
| 1 | the root law, one spelling | (b′) | 2.5 | 0 |
| 2 | the fragment door walls itself | (b′) residue | 1.0 | 1 |
| 3 | the group arrives whole | (d′) | 4.0 | nothing (may run parallel to 1–2) |
| 4 | the member's death named | (c′) | 2.5 | ''the operator's ruling'' |
| 5 | the ungated child | (b) | 4.0 | 1, and the echo law |
|  | ''total'' |  | ''15.5'' |  |


!! Refined by the house — 2026-09-12

The operator read the plan and sent the house back to sharpen it before the same hand enacts. Five refinements; none reopens a lean.

# ''Phase 4 moves up and merges with (d′-2).'' Under the ruling below (c′ = scar, marked), Phase 4 waits on nothing. The one template (`tiddlers/ahu-template-html.tid:4`) learns the THREE states of an empty body in ONE step — //unresolved// (no record at the child's address) · //arriving// (a record with no text) · //empty// (a record with empty text) — so (c′)'s mark and (d′)'s cord land together or not at all, as the table itself warned. New order: 0 · 1 · 4 · 2 · 3 · 5.
# ''Phase 0 gains the Muse's second catch as a red.'' `AHU_OPEN_RE` (`src/meme-ast/ahu-scan.ts:32`) swallows `kahea`, so `collectAhuSlots` (`:101`) counts a CALL as a DECLARED slot and the ahu-drop guard (`src/ingest-gate.ts:167-178`) reads the wrong set. Red: a root whose text carries `<<~ kahea ahu #/b>>` and no `<<~ ahu #/b>>` block yields NO declared slot from `collectAhuSlots`; CONTROL: a true `<<~ ahu #/b>>` block still counts. Cure in the scanner, never in the guard. +1.0 h.
# ''The anti-stall CONTROL rides EVERY e2e phase'', not Phase 1 alone: after each phase's vector, a later save lands its own 2xx — the one assertion that proves `syncer.js:436` did not fire. Phases 2 and 3 both touch paths the syncer drives.
# ''The contract line for the lab.'' `docs/pono/meme-api-surface.mem` gains one sentence under the two doors: //a slot child is a tiddler; the native door lands it as one, ungated, and the root re-cuts on the server — a child's save never addresses `/memes/`//. Stranger's sentence, written where the QA lab reads. +0.5 h, in Phase 1's aftermath.
# ''Phase 3's dial is named now.'' `$:/config/lares/memes/fat-children` (default `yes`): the skin re-inflates children only while it reads yes; the before/after byte size is reported in the commit body so the dial gets ruled against a number.

Total: ''17.0 spirit-hours.''

!! Moʻolelo — the eight answers, ruled 2026-09-12

<<~ moolelo held="(1) (c′) = SCAR, MARKED — the crossroads' answer; keep the pointer, mark it dead; never-invent-bytes rules · (2) no re-cut, so no 412 on a party who did nothing · (3) the pasted frame stays as AUTHORED TEXT; the grade speaks in Phase 5 · (4) the payload gets a dial, `$:/config/lares/memes/fat-children` default yes, with the measured size reported · (5) (d′) IS a defect for this house's carriers (eleven-slot documents are the normal); Phase 3 stands whole · (6) `<<~?` waits its own pass; unbound here · (7) a child's save IS graded, through the root re-place · (8) order 0 · 1 · 4 · 2 · 3 · 5 — (b′) first, the human's screen second, arrival third, the ungated child last (operator, on the house's answers)">>the same hand that sat the table enacts, red-first, every phase with its anti-stall control<<~/moolelo>>

