<<~ ahu #/questions>>

! The questions only the operator answers

''Lares (Council).'' Ordered so the answers unblock the plan in the order the plan needs them.

# ''(c′) — scar or re-cut?'' Does a member's death leave the call standing (the crossroads' answer: keep the pointer, mark it dead) or re-cut the root from its remaining children? Everything in Phase 4 waits on this one word.
# ''If re-cut — is the concurrency cost acceptable?'' Deleting one section moves the ROOT's canonical hash, so every unrelated in-flight edit of the same carrier answers 412. The party who pays did nothing. Does the house accept that trade for tidiness?
# ''(b′) after Phase 1 — what happens to the frame an author pasted into a child?'' It lands verbatim and `expandRefs` splices it into the root's render: a frame inside a frame. Three answers: STRIP the frame at the child's door · KEEP it as authored text and let the grade speak (Phase 5) · RE-PLACE the whole save under the root (b′-5, with its concurrency cost). The plan assumes KEEP; say so if it is wrong.
# ''(d′) — does the payload cross a line?'' Phase 3 makes every poll carry every meme's children. Does that want a dial (a `$:/config` the operator turns), a cap (fatten below N bytes), or nothing? Phase 3 will report the measured size before and after; the dial is a ruling, not a measurement.
# ''(d′) — is it a defect at all?'' The window is N HTTP round trips, N = the group's size: invisible on a loopback, several seconds on a café connection with a long carrier. If the answer is "a window that settles is not a defect", Phase 3 becomes (d′-2) alone and drops from 4 hours to 1.
# ''`<<~?`'' — does the unresolved-pressure register get ruled and bound in its own pass, or stay reserved? Phase 4's render step works either way; the question is whether the house wants the mark in the SERVED TEXT and not only on the page.
# ''(b) — should a slot child's save be graded at all?'' Phase 5 assumes yes (the backstop re-places the root, which grades the whole). The other reading: a child is a fragment of a carrier, never a carrier, and grading belongs at the root's own save alone — in which case Phase 5 is not a widening but a deletion of the question.
# ''Phase ordering'' — Breach-Watch ranked (b′) first because it writes an unreadable record silently. If the operator's own pressure is elsewhere — the phone vessel, the mesh — Phases 3 and 4 detach cleanly and 1+2 can stand alone as the whole pass.

