!! Retirement

This floor retires by the rite (fold · weld · one last check-in · delete). Folded already: phases 0·1·4·2·3 into <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/syncer-back-parity">> `#/leans`. Blocking: seam (b) — Phase 5's refutation (`3dfb06170`) stands without a ruling (a child's save grades against its OWN authored text, or a child reads ungraded by law).

''The seam's DECISION SURFACE stands built and the ruling still waits'': <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/child-grade-decision">> carries the ontology, the grade followed to its two `error` legs, both forks with their losing cases, the consequence ladder, three humans, the collision against standing law, and seventeen measured rows. It presents; it rules nothing. ''What it settles by measure'': standing law already forbids REFUSING a child's save (a 4xx stalls the stock queue), so the open word names whether the reading gets spoken, never whether the bytes land. ''What it surfaces'': the paste that opened seam (b) grades `clean` on the child's own bytes and shows as `2 text frames` in `readCarrierShape` over the ROOT's served render — so the fault composes at the join and neither fork's altitude reads it.

''TWO inbound edges to weld, and they want DIFFERENT welds.'' Measured 2026-09-13 — re-derive with `grep -rn "syncer-seams-roundtable" --include='*.mem' . | grep -v node_modules | grep -v "docs/pono/syncer-seams-roundtable.mem"`, which returns four `loulou` sites across three carriers (the fourth being the decision surface's own `#/edges`, which re-points for free):

* `syncer-back-parity.mem:164` points a reader here //for the argument and the plan// — a weld MOVES that content or RE-POINTS the sentence.
* `otakiage.mem:382` cites this floor as the worked example of ''`standing` × `floor`, nearly foldable'', and `:449` carries the same carrier's outbound edge. That first row wants a ''replacement exemplar'' rather than a re-point: deleting this carrier deletes the evidence the stage names something real. ⚠ `otakiage:383` immediately below leans on `scale-stories-basket-one` for the neighbouring `folded` stage, so ''both of that table's exemplars sit in the retirement queue at once'' — a rite whose worked examples retire faster than the rite documents them.

A fourth reference stands in code at `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/root-law-one-spelling.test.ts:4`, a header comment naming this floor's Phase 0. It carries no edge and welds nothing, and it re-points cheaply — but a hand deleting this carrier should know the comment names a file that will not exist.

